From: Shirogane Tsumugi <artoriapendragon123@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: skip SATAPWR/MACPWR setup when the pin is unset

SATAPWR and MACPWR are Kconfig strings. Leaving them blank still yields
`#define CONFIG_SATAPWR ""`, which satisfies #ifdef, so board_init always
runs the block: sunxi_name_to_gpio("") returns -1, both gpio calls fail,
and mdelay(500) still happens.

Only request, drive, and wait when the name resolves to a
real pin -- the same approach mainline U-Boot uses.

--- a/board/sunxi/board.c
+++ b/board/sunxi/board.c
@@ -261,15 +261,19 @@
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_SATAPWR
 	satapwr_pin = sunxi_name_to_gpio(CONFIG_SATAPWR);
-	gpio_request(satapwr_pin, "satapwr");
-	gpio_direction_output(satapwr_pin, 1);
-	/* Give attached sata device time to power-up to avoid link timeouts */
-	mdelay(500);
+	if (satapwr_pin >= 0) {
+		gpio_request(satapwr_pin, "satapwr");
+		gpio_direction_output(satapwr_pin, 1);
+		/* Give attached sata device time to power-up to avoid link timeouts */
+		mdelay(500);
+	}
 #endif
 #ifdef CONFIG_MACPWR
 	macpwr_pin = sunxi_name_to_gpio(CONFIG_MACPWR);
-	gpio_request(macpwr_pin, "macpwr");
-	gpio_direction_output(macpwr_pin, 1);
+	if (macpwr_pin >= 0) {
+		gpio_request(macpwr_pin, "macpwr");
+		gpio_direction_output(macpwr_pin, 1);
+	}
 #endif
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_DM_I2C
